      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Postmyocardial infarction patients with angina of new onset showed increased blood levels of fibrinogens, soluble fibrin and fibrinogen-fibrin degradation products one month after the acute onset of MI, while their baseline fibrinolysis had been normal. A variety of fibrinolytic disorders were revealed in response to physical stress."},
